    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nKevin Beirne Auctioneers are delighted to present No. 129 Manor Village, Westport Road, Castlebar, Co. Mayo to the open market for sale.\n\nThis attractive three-bedroom semi-detached property is ideally situated within the highly regarded Manor Village residential development, enjoying an excellent position overlooking a large communal green area.\n\nManor Village is a very popular residential estate, predominantly owner-occupied, and is conveniently located just a short distance from Castlebar town centre and a wide range of local amenities. The property is also within easy reach of Mayo General Hospital, secondary and national schools, ATU Mayo and the GMIT campus, shops, restaurants and a host of other services.\n\nNo. 129 is presented in very good condition both internally and externally and offers generous living accommodation throughout. The property also benefits from a private, mature rear garden and a tarmac driveway to the front.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall 15' x 6.5'\n\nWelcoming entrance hall with ceramic tiled flooring. Timber stairs lead to the first floor and landing.\n\nLiving Room 16' x 12'\n\nA spacious and bright living room with laminated timber flooring, open fireplace, curtains, TV point and double radiator. Double French doors provide direct access to the kitchen/dining area.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room 18' x 12'\n\nGenerous open-plan kitchen and dining space with ceramic tiled flooring and ample room for both kitchen and dining furniture. Patio doors lead directly to the rear garden.\n\nDownstairs WC\n\nWC and wash-hand basin with tiled flooring.\n\nFirst Floor\nMaster Bedroom 15' x 14'\n\nA spacious master bedroom with timber flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\nEn-suite: Fully tiled from floor to ceiling and incorporating shower, WC and wash-hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 11' x 10'\n\nGood-sized double bedroom with timber flooring and fitted wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 3 8' x 9'\n\nBedroom with timber flooring and fitted wardrobe.\n\nOutside\n\nThe property is approached via a tarmac driveway with attractive front garden area.\n\nTo the rear is a mature, private garden, with boundaries clearly defined by a black wall. There is also a separate black garage housing the oil burner.\n\nThe property enjoys an excellent position within Manor Village, close to the estate entrance and directly overlooking the substantial communal green area."
      },
